{"id": "EUVD-2026-41494", "enisaUuid": "3daf67a8-89be-3845-a3ef-83f7194291db", "description": "A vulnerability in libcurl caused the HTTP `Referer:` header to persist even\nwhen explicitly cleared. While the documentation states that passing NULL to\n`CURLOPT_REFERER` suppresses the header, the option failed to clear the\ninternal state. As a result, the previous referrer string was erroneously\nreused and sent in subsequent requests, potentially leaking sensitive\ninformation to unintended servers.", "datePublished": "2026-07-03T06:18:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-15T06:03:33", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://curl.se/docs/CVE-2026-9546.json", "https://curl.se/docs/CVE-2026-9546.html", "https://hackerone.com/reports/3754343"], "aliases": ["GHSA-25rx-86v8-32c6", "CVE-2026-9546"], "assigner": "curl", "epss": 0.65, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "425ff32b-76a2-3db1-80ae-019fcdf8dbd4", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.20.0"}, {"id": "8c016193-8de1-317a-b96c-671293d4fdfd", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.19.0"}, {"id": "9b08407a-c33d-33f9-9ef0-b55fc0c638ca", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.18.0"}, {"id": "bace4b73-a892-3fac-b55e-1222182e3645", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.18.0 <8.20.1"}, {"id": "eba03369-58f6-3f28-8d08-4661546de9ad", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "2cb868242dc2ac9cd52ee64987ef51d5964a56f9 <862e8a74a84478d82973471b4f49dc2746c1780e"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a5b128be-77d7-3ea1-911a-d6d5c279e35a", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}], "isExploited": false}